WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.921
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.221 --> 00:00:08.212
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.512 --> 00:00:15.565
Unit four: Leadership. In this unit, you will analyse different leadership styles and qualities.

4
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.493
visionary.

5
00:00:18.193 --> 00:00:23.060
visionary means having a clear, inspiring idea of the future.

6
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.378
She is a visionary leader who saw the potential of online learning early.

7
00:00:29.078 --> 00:00:32.137
Your turn. Say: visionary.

8
00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:35.803
visionary.

9
00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:37.841
delegation.

10
00:00:38.541 --> 00:00:42.955
delegation means giving tasks and responsibility to other people.

11
00:00:43.255 --> 00:00:46.637
Good delegation frees leaders to focus on strategy.

12
00:00:47.337 --> 00:00:50.256
Your turn. Say: delegation.

13
00:00:52.956 --> 00:00:53.980
delegation.

14
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:57.203
decision-making.

15
00:00:57.903 --> 00:01:02.004
decision-making means the process of choosing between options.

16
00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:04.734
Clear data improves decision-making.

17
00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:09.003
Your turn. Say: decision-making.

18
00:01:11.703 --> 00:01:14.028
decision-making.

19
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:15.960
charisma.

20
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:21.631
charisma means a strong personal charm that attracts and influences people.

21
00:01:21.931 --> 00:01:24.674
His charisma made everyone want to follow him.

22
00:01:25.374 --> 00:01:28.003
Your turn. Say: charisma.

23
00:01:30.703 --> 00:01:31.553
charisma.

24
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.876
servant leadership.

25
00:01:34.576 --> 00:01:40.779
servant leadership means a style where the leader focuses on helping the team grow.

26
00:01:41.079 --> 00:01:44.018
Servant leadership builds loyalty and trust.

27
00:01:44.718 --> 00:01:47.986
Your turn. Say: servant leadership.

28
00:01:50.686 --> 00:01:52.070
servant leadership.

29
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:54.224
micromanage.

30
00:01:54.924 --> 00:01:58.955
micromanage means to control every small detail of other people's work.

31
00:01:59.255 --> 00:02:01.998
Nobody likes a boss who micromanages.

32
00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:06.256
Your turn. Say: micromanage.

33
00:02:08.956 --> 00:02:10.073
micromanage.

34
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:12.340
consensus.

35
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.980
consensus means general agreement among a group.

36
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.347
The team reached a consensus after a long discussion.

37
00:02:20.047 --> 00:02:23.280
Your turn. Say: consensus.

38
00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.086
consensus.

39
00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:29.526
inspire trust.

40
00:02:30.226 --> 00:02:34.199
inspire trust means to make people believe in you and rely on you.

41
00:02:34.499 --> 00:02:37.892
Honest leaders inspire trust even in difficult times.

42
00:02:38.592 --> 00:02:41.743
Your turn. Say: inspire trust.

43
00:02:44.443 --> 00:02:45.932
inspire trust.

44
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:49.125
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:49.425 --> 00:02:52.133
Rithy, what do you think makes a great leader?

46
00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:58.995
It's not charisma that matters most. What really counts is the ability to inspire trust.

47
00:03:00.283 --> 00:03:04.190
Interesting. Many people would say charisma is essential.

48
00:03:05.483 --> 00:03:10.548
Charisma helps, but it was my first manager's honesty that made me respect her.

49
00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.339
Was she a visionary?

50
00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.859
Not really. What she did brilliantly was delegation. She never micromanaged us.

51
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.173
That sounds like servant leadership.

52
00:03:24.483 --> 00:03:30.119
Exactly. All she wanted was for the team to grow, and we reached consensus easily.

53
00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:34.809
Grammar focus: Advanced cleft sentences.

54
00:03:35.109 --> 00:03:39.187
Advanced cleft sentences help you emphasise exactly what you want.

55
00:03:39.487 --> 00:03:44.134
What really counts is, it was something that, and all she wanted was.

56
00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:48.152
For example: It was her honesty that made me respect her.

57
00:03:48.452 --> 00:03:53.516
Cleft sentences let you control emphasis in speeches, essays and debates.

58
00:03:54.517 --> 00:03:58.226
Now read and listen. The Quiet Power of Servant Leaders.

59
00:03:58.526 --> 00:04:03.428
For decades, leadership was associated with charisma, confidence and command.

60
00:04:04.717 --> 00:04:11.441
However, research increasingly shows that the most effective leaders are often quiet and humble.

61
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.781
What these leaders share is a focus on helping their teams succeed.

62
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:22.451
This style, known as servant leadership, puts the needs of employees first.

63
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:29.209
Servant leaders delegate responsibility instead of trying to micromanage every task.

64
00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:34.467
They also involve their teams in decision-making and look for consensus.

65
00:04:35.783 --> 00:04:39.582
It is this sense of respect that inspires trust and loyalty.

66
00:04:40.883 --> 00:04:46.343
In a fast-changing world, the best leaders may be those who listen more than they speak.

67
00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.151
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:04:50.451 --> 00:04:53.635
Giving tasks and responsibility to others is blank.

69
00:04:53.935 --> 00:04:58.773
A, delegation. B, charisma. C, consensus.

70
00:05:02.783 --> 00:05:05.398
The answer is A: delegation.

71
00:05:06.883 --> 00:05:08.999
blank I need is a little more time.

72
00:05:09.299 --> 00:05:12.116
A, What. B, It. C, That.

73
00:05:16.117 --> 00:05:18.256
The answer is A: What.

74
00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.713
It was the coach blank changed the team's attitude.

75
00:05:23.013 --> 00:05:26.388
A, what. B, who. C, which.

76
00:05:30.383 --> 00:05:32.325
The answer is B: who.

77
00:05:33.817 --> 00:05:37.372
To control every small detail of others' work is to blank.

78
00:05:37.672 --> 00:05:43.276
A, inspire trust. B, micromanage. C, delegate.

79
00:05:47.283 --> 00:05:50.014
The answer is B: micromanage.

80
00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:55.118
According to the text, what do servant leaders put first?

81
00:05:55.418 --> 00:06:00.883
A, profit. B, the needs of employees. C, their own image.

82
00:06:04.883 --> 00:06:08.323
The answer is B: the needs of employees.

83
00:06:09.817 --> 00:06:14.605
Now it's your turn. Part one: What kind of leader would you like to be?

84
00:06:19.905 --> 00:06:25.399
Part two: Explain two qualities you value and describe a leader you admire.

85
00:06:31.699 --> 00:06:44.687
What I'd most like to be is a servant leader. I value honesty and good delegation. It was my high-school teacher who showed me this: she trusted us with real responsibility, and we never wanted to let her down.

86
00:06:44.987 --> 00:06:47.149
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:53.171
Great work today! You learned eight new words and advanced cleft sentences.

88
00:06:53.471 --> 00:06:57.040
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

89
00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.016
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

90
00:07:00.316 --> 00:07:02.759
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

